main/doctest: don't build the bundled tests/examples.

doctest is header-only; the package ships only headers + CMake config.
The bundled examples compile with -Werror (set by doctest's own example
CMakeLists), and clang 22 introduces -Wc2y-extensions which fires on
doctest's use of __COUNTER__ — 20+ errors, build dies. Chimera's binary
repos still carry a pre-clang-22 build, so this is latent upstream until
their next doctest rebuild.

Disabling DOCTEST_WITH_TESTS skips the examples (nothing packaged from
them). Alternative considered: appending -Wno-c2y-extensions to CXXFLAGS;
rejected since building test binaries for a header-only package is wasted
work in the first place (and cross builds never run them).

--- a/main/doctest/template.py
+++ b/main/doctest/template.py
@@ -3,6 +3,7 @@ pkgver = "2.4.12"
 pkgrel = 0
 build_style = "cmake"
 configure_args = [
+    "-DDOCTEST_WITH_TESTS=OFF",
     "-DDOCTEST_USE_STD_HEADERS=ON",
 ]
 hostmakedepends = [
